Source: https://github.com/lz4/lz4
Tag: v1.9.4
Commit: 5ff839680134437dbf4678f3d0c7b371d84f4964
License: BSD-2-Clause (see LICENSE and the source file headers).

The block codec is built through the legacy Linux 3.4 adapters one level up.
lz4_compat.h selects the upstream freestanding API, compiler builtins for
memory operations, private static linkage, and forced inline for GNU89.
No allocation or streaming API is exported to the rest of this kernel.

Changes to the imported sources:
- lz4.h uses linux/types.h under __KERNEL__; its C99 stdint branch is disabled
  in kernel builds. The deprecated allocator declaration is guarded in the
  same way as its disabled implementation.
- lz4.c avoids libc limits.h/stdint.h under __KERNEL__. Linux already assumes
  a 32-bit int, so its userspace UINT_MAX preprocessor check is skipped.
- Four internal functions in lz4.c use LZ4LIB_API to inherit the adapter's
  private linkage, avoiding duplicate global symbols between legacy objects.
- lz4hc.c, lz4hc.h and LICENSE are unchanged from the tag.

The Linux-facing lz4_compress/lz4hc_compress APIs retain the original
requirement that the destination hold lz4_compressbound(src_len) bytes.
The normal compressor uses acceleration 1; HC uses the upstream default
level 9. zRAM still selects the normal compressor.

Workspace sizes are 16416 bytes for LZ4 and 262200 bytes for LZ4 HC. The
adapters check the sizes at compile time. Rebuild every caller with the
updated include/linux/lz4.h; do not mix these objects with old modules.
